  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:causal-transfer",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\) and \\(a\\in J\\), define\n\\[\n h_n(a)=\\left\\{\\frac{4\\kappa(a)}{n f(a)\\theta'(a)^2}\\right\\}^{1/3}.\n\\]\nThen \\(h_n(a)>0\\) and, uniformly in \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\) and \\(a\\in J\\),\n\\[\n \\left(\\frac{4v_\\kappa}{C_gC_\\theta^2}\\right)^{1/3}\n \\le n^{1/3}h_n(a)\n \\le\n \\left(\\frac{4V_\\kappa}{c_gc_\\theta^2}\\right)^{1/3}.\n\\]\nThe coordinate\n\\[\n \\Psi_{n,P}(a)=\\int_{\\inf J}^{a}h_n(v)^{-1}\\,dv\n\\]\nis bi-Lipschitz and maps \\(J\\) onto an interval of exact length\n\\[\n \\Psi_{n,P}(\\sup J)=n^{1/3}\\int_J\n \\left\\{\\frac{f(a)\\theta'(a)^2}{4\\kappa(a)}\\right\\}^{1/3}da\n =T_n(P).\n\\]\nThis is an exact spatial-clock identity; it does not assert a coupling of \\(S_n\\) or \\(S_n^\\circ\\) to a canonical growing-domain maximum.",
    "depends_on": [
      "def:model-class",
      "def:spatial-clock",
      "ass:p-normalization",
      "ass:overlap",
      "ass:strict-slope",
      "ass:variance"
    ],
    "justification": "Derives the exact local cube-root scale and spatial-volume clock under explicit positivity conditions.",
    "gap": "No growing-domain coupling or cross-fitted optimized-value stability is proved.",
    "consumer": "The clock is an algebraic coordinate, not an observed-statistic limit theorem.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\) and \\(a\\in J\\).  By \\(\\texttt{ass:p-normalization}\\), \\(\\int p(w)\\,dw=1\\), and by \\(\\texttt{ass:overlap}\\),\n\\[\n c_g\\le g(a\\mid w)\\le C_g\n\\]\nfor every \\(w\\in[0,1]^d\\).  Since \\(p\\ge0\\), the definition of \\(f\\) therefore gives\n\\[\n c_g=c_g\\int p(w)\\,dw\n \\le f(a)=\\int g(a\\mid w)p(w)\\,dw\n \\le C_g\\int p(w)\\,dw=C_g. \\tag{1}\n\\]\nThe assumptions \\(\\texttt{ass:strict-slope}\\) and \\(\\texttt{ass:variance}\\) give\n\\[\n 0<c_\\theta\\le\\theta'(a)\\le C_\\theta,\n \\qquad\n 0<v_\\kappa\\le\\kappa(a)\\le V_\\kappa. \\tag{2}\n\\]\nThus every quantity divided by in the definition of \\(h_n(a)\\) is strictly positive, so \\(h_n(a)>0\\).  Combining (1)--(2), and taking cube roots only after division by positive quantities, yields\n\\[\n \\left(\\frac{4v_\\kappa}{nC_gC_\\theta^2}\\right)^{1/3}\n \\le h_n(a)\\le\n \\left(\\frac{4V_\\kappa}{nc_gc_\\theta^2}\\right)^{1/3}. \\tag{3}\n\\]\nMultiplication by \\(n^{1/3}>0\\) proves the asserted uniform bounds on \\(n^{1/3}h_n(a)\\).\n\nInverting the positive defining expression gives\n\\[\n h_n(a)^{-1}=n^{1/3}\n \\left\\{\\frac{f(a)\\theta'(a)^2}{4\\kappa(a)}\\right\\}^{1/3}. \\tag{4}\n\\]\nTaking reciprocals in (3) bounds the right-hand side of (4) between\n\\[\n n^{1/3}\\left(\\frac{c_gc_\\theta^2}{4V_\\kappa}\\right)^{1/3}\n \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n n^{1/3}\\left(\\frac{C_gC_\\theta^2}{4v_\\kappa}\\right)^{1/3}. \\tag{5}\n\\]\nFor \\(a_1<a_2\\) in \\(J\\), integration of (5) gives\n\\[\n n^{1/3}\\left(\\frac{c_gc_\\theta^2}{4V_\\kappa}\\right)^{1/3}(a_2-a_1)\n \\le \\Psi_{n,P}(a_2)-\\Psi_{n,P}(a_1)\n \\le n^{1/3}\\left(\\frac{C_gC_\\theta^2}{4v_\\kappa}\\right)^{1/3}(a_2-a_1). \\tag{6}\n\\]\nBoth bounding constants are finite and strictly positive.  Hence \\(\\Psi_{n,P}\\) is strictly increasing and Lipschitz on \\(J\\), and (6) also makes its inverse Lipschitz on its image.  Thus it is bi-Lipschitz.  Since \\(\\Psi_{n,P}(\\inf J)=0\\), the image is an interval of length \\(\\Psi_{n,P}(\\sup J)\\).  Integrating (4) and invoking \\(\\texttt{def:spatial-clock}\\) proves\n\\[\n \\Psi_{n,P}(\\sup J)\n =n^{1/3}\\int_J\n \\left\\{\\frac{f(a)\\theta'(a)^2}{4\\kappa(a)}\\right\\}^{1/3}\\,da\n =n^{1/3}\\mathcal V(P)=T_n(P). \\tag{7}\n\\]\nAll constants in (3), (5), and (6) depend only on the fixed model constants, so the bounds are uniform over \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\) and \\(a\\in J\\).  The derivation is an exact observed-law coordinate identity and makes no coupling claim for an observed likelihood-ratio statistic.",
